A||||10||KnightRyder31||1991 Eagle Talon TSI||||1||
Z||000000||KnightRyder31||07-13-2001||11:41 PM||||I just test drove an Eagle Talon AWD Turbo 5-speed!<BR>Boy was I suprised how quick that thing was!<BR>It felt like it did 0-60 in the mid 6 sec. range!<BR>It could probably do the 1/4 mile in like 15 secs!<BR>The car was very fun to drive, had it going like 90MPH, and it got there in no time!<BR>This guy is selling this baby for like $2,800... and it seems like a pretty good deal. The only thing bad about it is the high amount of miles (120,000)!<BR>It runs very well though, so I'm gonna try to by her!<BR>I hope I can get the funds together for this.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||07-14-2001||12:42 AM||||careful, those things go through timing belts like no-one's business.  Make sure he's kept up on maintenance.  One of my friends got one a while ago and the turbo blew.. now it's just sitting.<P>Don't get me wrong, they're sweet cars.  I'd love to have one!<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||07-14-2001||08:30 AM||||I had a 92 AWD turbo Laser- turbo went at 50K (fortunately still under warranty). Do a compression check, it's very common to need head work at about 75K also the 2nd to 3rd syncros have trouble. Also if the timing belt goes it destroys the valves(interference engine). The only recalls that I know about(at least for the 92's) were one for the timing belt and one for the transfer case seal. And I even think the wheels fit a Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000003||00lE||07-14-2001||01:49 PM||||I believe one of the biggest issues with the DSM 2.0 was a problem called "crank walk".  Not sure how to determine if this is present, but someone at dsm.org could probably help.  The manual transmissions are also known to be a weak link, and they are quite expensive to replace.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula||07-14-2001||02:51 PM||||crank walk is only on the 94 and up ones... and the biggest complaints are the timing belt breaking causes $2000 in damage and the trannies break all the time.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigformulagt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mach10||07-14-2001||03:11 PM||||Personally, I'd never buy one in Winnipeg. Every one that I've seen has been BAGGED. The engine/trans combo is not very strong. Yes they're quick. So was the Masserati Bi-Turbo. (The only car that came factory with a separate parts car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">).<BR>Sorry, I'm just not a fan. They look awesome, and handle pretty nice, but they don't stand up to much pressure before blowing something.||||reg||13
Z||000006||Black88GT||07-14-2001||05:44 PM||||Yeah I think they are more trouble then they are worth.  My brother had a '97 or '98 GS-T Spyder.  Went through tranny's like no tomorrow.  When the top was down the car felt like it was going to fall apart.  It was fast but not blazing.  <P>Another story, my co-worker has a Talon, last year they made them (think its a '97) but its not a turbo.  Eats timing belts, and those aren't cheap.  But I don't think that it ruins the valves when they break cuz she has went through a few of them.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||danny boy||07-14-2001||08:18 PM||||We've had ours for 3+ years.111000 miles,50K when bought. Things I've had to replace:<BR>brakes<BR>right rear wheel bearing<BR>crank pulley(freak occurance and my fault)<BR>left rear brake light bulb<BR> This car does not have an easy life. Half of everyone I know has these things, and I've never seen a 15 second DSM.||||reg||1
Z||000008||The Fieromaster||07-15-2001||12:20 AM||||Crakn walk is a problem but only on the second gens...<P>as for 1/4 times... 15 my A$$!  My 97 GSX Eclipse (awd turbo) could pull it off in around 14.3!  That was a great car... oh well.. Its nothin but scrap metal now!<P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That, Wrecked Better"<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">      <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>AIM: Fieromaster<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||1
Z||000009||GT Bastard||07-15-2001||02:11 PM||||I've got a '91 Talon Tsi AWD 5sp project in the works... I've been around a few of these cars, and YES they're a pain to maintain.  Trannies, timing belts, turbos.... But can they move?  Hell yes!!! The performance potential for these cars is un-godly for a 2.0 4cyl.  If you can work on it yourself, I'd say go for it.  If not, that car will eat you alive.... A stock '91 Talon awd, 5sp does the 1/4 in 14.7 seconds in most sources.  Making them 13 second cars is hardly a challenge.  <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gtbastard.gif">     <P>"My heroes are John Wayne, the Simpsons, and whoever canceled Full House/Bob Saget."||||reg||1
Z||000010||KnightRyder31||07-15-2001||07:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GT Bastard:<BR><B>I've got a '91 Talon Tsi AWD 5sp project in the works... I've been around a few of these cars, and YES they're a pain to maintain.  Trannies, timing belts, turbos.... But can they move?  Hell yes!!! The performance potential for these cars is un-godly for a 2.0 4cyl.  If you can work on it yourself, I'd say go for it.  If not, that car will eat you alive.... A stock '91 Talon awd, 5sp does the 1/4 in 14.7 seconds in most sources.  Making them 13 second cars is hardly a challenge.  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>My thoughts exactly!<BR>Thank you.<BR>||||reg||1
